339	675,1005,1745,1565	339. Twig of Grape-vine.	A length of grape-vine stem with two deeply lobed, toothed leaves and several tendrils, some coiled into tight springs and one twisted round a stalk.
340	160,1315,345,1555	340. Flower opening.	A tiny grape flower opening: the five petals still cohering at the top and lifting away from the base like a cap.
341	365,1315,560,1555	341. Same, with the petals fallen.	The same flower after the petals have fallen, showing five spreading stamens around the short pistil in the little cup of the calyx.
342	145,1770,485,2060	342. Flowers of a Buckthorn.	A Buckthorn flower seen from above: pointed calyx lobes, small petals each with a stamen before it, and a fleshy disk round the centre.
343	480,1810,775,2045	343. Same, cut through lengthwise.	The flower cut through lengthwise, showing the stamens and petals set on the calyx tube and the ovary sitting in the cup.
